## Goal
Write a short markdown memo for the Platform team weekly meeting of Monday 12 October 2026, covering exactly the decisions made and every commitment (including informal ones) from the notes file. Nothing invented.

## Acceptance criteria
C1: The memo is markdown and has at most 400 words as counted by read.
C2: It covers only the meeting in the given notes file.
C3: It has a Decisions section that lists every decision recorded in the notes file and no decision that is not in the notes.
C4: It has an action-items table with exactly the columns Owner | Action | Due, with one row for every commitment in the notes, including informal ones where a person said in prose that they would do something, and no row that is not in the notes.
C5: Every Due value is an ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD) or none. A relative deadline (for example next week, next meeting) becomes a date only when the notes make the date clear; otherwise Due is none. No date is guessed.
C6: Every owner name matches the person named in the notes.
C7: (reviewer's criterion — not applicable to writer)
C8: The memo starts with a one-line summary of the meeting that begins with 'Summary:', followed by the Decisions section, followed by the action-items table, in that order.

STRUCTURE (mandatory, in this exact order):
1. First line: a single line starting with 'Summary:' that summarises the meeting in a single sentence, using only information from the notes file.
2. Decisions section.
3. Action-items table with columns Owner | Action | Due.
4. A 'Next meeting' footer if stated in the notes.
No other sections (no Open Questions, no notes, nothing else).

Date resolution guidance (C5):
- Explicit dates like 'Oct 14', 'Oct 16', 'Oct 20' resolve to 2026-10-14, 2026-10-16, 2026-10-20.
- 'The day before the freeze starts' with the freeze on Oct 22 resolves to 2026-10-21.
- If a date cannot be calculated from the notes, use none.

Deliverable: one markdown file named memo-2026-10-12.md, saved as lead/writer/work/memo-2026-10-12.md.

